WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.700
That rumor about Kevin Costner and "Yellowstone"&nbsp;
is an "absolute lie" … according to the star's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.580
lawyer. But what do Costner's&nbsp;
co-stars have to say about it?

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.720
After struggling in Los Angeles in a&nbsp;
series of odd jobs, Kevin Costner won&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.560
roles in several B-movies before making&nbsp;
it big in the late '80s with roles in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.520
hit films "The Untouchables," "Bull Durham"&nbsp;
and "Field of Dreams." The actor sat in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.000
director's chair for 1990's "Dances&nbsp;
with Wolves" and went on to win two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.660
Academy Awards for Best Director and Best&nbsp;
Picture as one of the Western's producers.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.460
After a few major flops, he kept a relatively&nbsp;
low profile for a Hollywood A-lister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.000
but in 2018, Costner turned his&nbsp;
skills to the small screen with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.900
his role as family patriarch John Dutton in&nbsp;
Taylor Sheridan's hit drama "Yellowstone."

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.440
His performance is one of the boldest&nbsp;
and most enigmatic of his long career,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.040
with his co-stars at one time offering&nbsp;
praise for the veteran performer's on-set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.000
behavior. But these compliments grew few and&nbsp;
far between as the fifth season of the drama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.380
unfolded and Costner's behind-the-scenes actions&nbsp;
allegedly upset some of his fellow performers.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:01:00.300
According to a report by Puck, some of the&nbsp;
cast and crew has been, quote, "frustrated by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.220
[Costner's] ego and his unavailability for a few&nbsp;
years now," and rumor has it that "Yellowstone"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:10.020
could be on its last legs, thanks in part to a&nbsp;
standoff over Costner's very limited availability.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:14.940
According to the publication, Costner negotiated&nbsp;
that Season 5 would be filmed in two parts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.580
each with an abbreviated filming schedule. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.800
Costner came down with COVID-19 during principal&nbsp;
photography. It is alleged that the actor refused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.860
to prolong his shooting schedule to make&nbsp;
up for the delay due to his illness.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:33.600
"If it's progress you seek, do not vote&nbsp;
for me. I am the opposite of progress."

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.100
Instead, Costner noted to the cast and crew&nbsp;
that his window for filming had come to an end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.440
and thus forced his fellow actors to reconvene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.991
months later to shoot his scenes again&nbsp;
— thereby eating into their schedules.

00:01:43.991 --> 00:01:46.380
This is also the claim made by Taylor Sheridan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.400
but Costner disputes the allegations entirely&nbsp;
and claims he was only following the terms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.940
of his contract. According to Marty&nbsp;
Singer, one of Costner's attorneys,

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.160
"The idea that Kevin was only willing to work one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.880
week on the second half of Season 5 of&nbsp;
'Yellowstone' is an absolute lie. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:03.453
ridiculous — and anyone suggesting it&nbsp;
shouldn't be believed for one second."

00:02:03.453 --> 00:02:07.500
The behind-the-scenes "Yellowstone" filming&nbsp;
schedule controversy is just one element of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:11.280
a greater portrait regarding Costner's strained&nbsp;
relationship with Taylor Sheridan's production.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:16.200
A report from Deadline indicated that Sheridan&nbsp;
was frustrated by Costner's limited availability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.789
for "Yellowstone" due to his commitment&nbsp;
to his own upcoming Western frontier saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.789 --> 00:02:23.525
"Horizon," which will be split into four&nbsp;
separate movies, according to Variety.

00:02:23.525 --> 00:02:27.000
The Deadline report further alleged&nbsp;
that Paramount was moving to conclude&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.460
"Yellowstone" at the end of its&nbsp;
fifth season before developing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.480
yet another spin-off — this time with Matthew&nbsp;
McConaughey as the lead rather than Costner.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.440
Deadline's report paints a grim picture&nbsp;
regarding the future of Costner's corner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.580
of the "Yellowstone" franchise, though several&nbsp;
other reputable sources have muddied the waters.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:45.900
Such a strategy conflicts with what star&nbsp;
Cole Hauser previously told Entertainment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.080
Tonight about the longevity of the&nbsp;
series and suggests that the issues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.440
surrounding Costner may have precipitated&nbsp;
Sheridan ending "Yellowstone" early.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.680
However, the Hollywood Reporter&nbsp;
spoke to sources who indicated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.951
that Costner departing would not mark an&nbsp;
immediate ending to the series. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.951 --> 00:03:04.080
Paramount Network has suggested that both&nbsp;
"Yellowstone" and Costner's role on the drama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:08.165
are both set to continue. A Paramount&nbsp;
Network spokesperson told Deadline,

00:03:08.165 --> 00:03:10.860
"We have no news to report.&nbsp;
Kevin Costner is a big part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.620
of 'Yellowstone' and we hope that's&nbsp;
the case for a long time to come."

